default-lease-time 30000 (in seconds) over 8 hours;
Default lease time refers to how long a device is granted access to a specific IP address by a DHCP server.
max-lease-time 72000 seconds 20 hours;
Max lease time is the upper limit set on a DHCP server for how long a device is allowed to keep a specific IP address before renewing it.
authorative -indicate the official dhcp server
subnet 192.168.1.0 netmask 255.255.255.0 - defines the network
range 192.168.1.100 192.168.1.200 - indicates the address available to clients
option routers 192.168.1.1 - default gateway
option subnet-mask 255.255.255.0 - shows the class of the network
option domain-name-servers 8.8.8.8 - identifies the dns server to use
option broadcast-address 192.168.1.255 - broadcast address
Validate the network configuration using dhcpd -t. No error shows that configuration was successful
systemctl enable isc-dhcp-server
systemctl status isc-dhcp-server
